# Cargo build tree — lives outside Maven's target/ (see pom.xml exec-maven-plugin
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR env var) so `mvn clean` doesn't blow away the Rust cache.
# Everything under here is regenerated by cargo build; never committed.
.cargo-target/

# Standard cargo target dir — used if cargo is invoked directly without the
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR override.
native/target/

# Native library outputs staged by the maven-antrun step into
# src/main/resources/natives/{platform}/ — these are regenerated by every
# build from the cargo output, so tracking them creates the stale-dylib
# landmine we hit in wasmtime4j (see local-dev profile discussion). The
# maven build's unpack-dependencies overlay is authoritative.
src/main/resources/natives/
